led with no arguments, returns nil. Per prd001-testutils R4.1 and R4.3.\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Primary exported type is DiffTest; primary source file is difftest.go (named after primary exported type, not package name, per project naming convention).\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Entry point signature is RunDiffTests(t *testing.T, goBinary string, refBinary string, tests []DiffTest) per prd001-testutils AC1.\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Timeout is implemented via context.WithTimeout wrapping exec.CommandContext; default is 10 seconds per prd001-testutils R2.3.\"\n      - id: D4\n        text: \"DiffTest.Normalize is []Normalize (a slice applied in order) per prd001-testutils R4.3. Nil or empty slice means no normalization is applied.\"\n      - id: D5\n        text: \"When DiffTest.WorkDir is empty, both binaries run in a per-test temporary directory created via t.TempDir() per prd001-testutils R2.5.\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"DiffTest struct and Normalize function type are defined with all fields specified in prd001-testutils R1.1-R1.4.\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"RunDiffTests(t, goBinary, refBinary, tests) is callable from a TestXxx function with no other setup per prd001-testutils AC1.\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"Binary execution captures stdout, stderr, and exit code independently. No output is written to the test process during a passing run per prd001-testutils R2.4.\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"Timeout defaults to 10 seconds. A DiffTest exceeding the timeout fails with a clear timeout message per prd001-testutils R2.3 and AC5.\"\n      - id: AC5\n        text: \"Comparison applies normalization then diffs byte-for-byte. Divergence report includes args, stdin (truncated to 256 bytes), both stdout, both stderr, and both exit codes per prd001-testutils R3.1-R3.5.\"\n      - id: AC6\n        text: \"TimestampNormalizer replaces strftime-formatted timestamps